      "math_academy_id": "q-88381",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274786/assets/fcdb1e3747dcba3067c9862d673af10fc71c4db5e19fe537fc1cdf8172f454bf.png)\n\nA stretch of factor $-2$ in the $x$-direction and $-2$ in the $y$-direction is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?",
      "worked_solution": "A stretch of factor $-2$ in the $x$-direction and $-2$ in the $y$-direction can be represented by the following function:\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-2x,-2y)\n$$\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our four vertices $(0,0)$, $(0,1)$, $(2,1)$, $(2,0)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0,0) & ↦((-2)\\cdot 0,\\,(-2)\\cdot 0)=(0,0) \\\\ (0,1) & ↦((-2)\\cdot 0,\\,(-2)\\cdot 1)=(0,-2) \\\\ (2,1) & ↦((-2)\\cdot 2,\\,(-2)\\cdot 1)=(-4,-2) \\\\ (2,0) & ↦((-2)\\cdot 2,\\,(-2)\\cdot 0)=(-4,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274786/assets/f31e9ef429f04f52ec448710a7d927ea032f57e6d1ff0bab2a996fc23f7c3865.png)",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
